From 20fbd0bc953aecb9474344606f922c0c106e1e23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:38:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mbaa: preload policy, ReadFile park contract, P8 palettes,
 census tool, HUD wait rates

Rebased onto the fork's main (c3f0474, 42 commits ahead of the 8e79a863 base
these changes were written against). Resolutions, all behavioural:

* src/09ad-handlers-d3d9.wat -- REAL ADDRESS COLLISION. The palettes were at
  +25616/+25620, which in this branch are the render-target slots 1-3 and
  pixel constants c8-c31 ($d3d9_color_binding_extra / $d3d9_float_constants),
  and lib/d3d9-host.js reads the render targets at those offsets. Overlaying
  them would have silently corrupted every render-target bind. The palettes
  now sit AFTER the historical device block, which ends at +26012:
    +26012 current palette number
    +26016 + 1024*n  16 palettes, through +42399
  d3d9_program_alloc grew 26012 -> 42400 to hold them.
* lib/d3d9-host.js -- keeps this branch's texture `identity` cache key (a mip
  record reused by a new texture must never match) AND the palette mark, so a
  P8 cache entry is keyed on both.
* lib/apps.js -- this branch's mbaa settings (audioThreadStepMs, fineQpc,
  d3d9FullNpot, d3d9PS20, native hook slots) kept alongside preloadAssets.
* lib/perf-hud.js -- sampler reads this branch's counters (heap, texture oom,
  native ftol) plus the two wait rates.

Verified on the merged tree: build 1769509 bytes, region hash 5d0cb5d37037987b,
all nine tests PASS.
