+### 2026-11-17: D3D9 texture palettes are real state
+
+242 -> 243 is the reverse direction, and it is a *metadata* stub being retired
+rather than a manual one added: `SetPaletteEntries`, `GetPaletteEntries`,
+`SetCurrentTexturePalette` and `GetCurrentTexturePalette` were straight-line
+returns (two of them through `$crash_unimplemented`), so an indexed
+(`D3DFMT_P8`) game was told "yes, palettes work" and then got a texture whose
+texels were the palette INDICES uploaded as greyscale — the white/light-grey
+sprite report. The device state now carries the 16 D3D9 palettes (256
+D3DCOLOR each) at `state+25620` and the current palette number at `state+25616`
+inside a 42000-byte allocation; the four handlers copy/store and
+`lib/d3d9-host.js` expands P8 through the palette that is current at upload
+time. The inventory count moves because four handlers are no longer quiet
+bodies; the digest is re-pinned by `node tools/check-silent-stubs.js --print`.
